{"v":1,"agent":"cursor","cli_version":"0.12.2","type":"assistant","content":[{"text":"I'll check how TipTap is set up today and what a custom block/template convention would take.","type":"text"},{"input":{"pattern":"canRoundTrip|extension|Node|shortcode|Slash|mdx|tiptap","path":"/Users/blaise/Developer/cms/web/src/modules/content","glob":"**/*.{ts,vue}","head_limit":50},"name":"Grep","type":"tool_use"},{"input":{"glob_pattern":"**/content/**/*.{ts,vue}","target_directory":"/Users/blaise/Developer/cms/web/src/modules"},"name":"Glob","type":"tool_use"},{"input":{"namespace":"cursor","toolName":"SwitchMode"},"name":"GetDynamicTools","type":"tool_use"},{"input":{"path":"/Users/blaise/Developer/cms/web/src/modules/content/markdown.ts","offset":95,"limit":80},"name":"Read","type":"tool_use"},{"input":{"path":"/Users/blaise/Developer/cms/web/src/modules/content/MarkdownBodyEditor.test.ts","offset":51,"limit":40},"name":"Read","type":"tool_use"},{"text":"Yes — but as a **small, allowlisted block convention**, not a general template language.\n\nToday TipTap rich mode only round-trips a fixed Markdown set. Anything that looks like HTML/MDX (`\u003c\u003e`, `{}`, imports) fails `canRoundTrip` and stays Raw. So “full Liquid/Handlebars/MDX in TipTap” is a no. A **custom CTA node** that TipTap understands end-to-end is a yes.\n\nWhat works well:\n\n1. **Source convention** — something TipTap + Astro both know, e.g.\n   ```md\n   :::cta\n   heading: Ready to launch?\n   label: Get started\n   href: /pricing\n   :::\n   ```\n   or a fenced block: ` ```cta ` with YAML attrs.\n\n2. **TipTap custom Node** — renders as a CTA card in the editor; slash command to insert; serialize/parse that exact syntax.\n\n3. **Site renderer** — remark plugin or MDX component that turns the same syntax into the real CTA.\n\nWhat does *not* work without a much bigger project: free-form `{{ ... }}`, arbitrary components, or “any template language.” You’d keep rejecting unknown tags so rich mode stays lossless.\n\n**Tradeoff:** frontmatter ordered sections stay simpler and don’t touch the body editor. A TipTap convention is better if writers need the CTA **inside** article flow and still want rich editing.\n\nIf you want to go ahead, next step is picking one syntax (`:::cta` vs fenced vs shortcode) and whether Astro should parse it in `.md` or only `.mdx`.","type":"text"}]}
